---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WindowPanel from '../components/WindowPanel.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../components/ProjectCard.astro';
import { projects } from '../data/projects';
---
<BaseLayout title="Projects" description="Open-source, hardware preservation, firmware research, and game development projects by Cole Pearson.">
  <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">/projects · mounted records</p><h1>Active files</h1><p>Software, hardware, dead media, and whatever rabbit hole looked interesting this week.</p></header>
  <div class="content-stack">
    <WindowPanel title="PROJECTS.DIR" class="project-panel" eyebrow="Featured work / sorted by priority"><div class="project-grid">{projects.map((project) => <div id={project.slug}><ProjectCard project={project} /></div>)}</div></WindowPanel>
    <WindowPanel title="README.TXT" class="readme-panel"><div class="prose"><p>Each project keeps its own identity. <strong>PLEASE REWIND</strong> belongs to the strange after-hours world of Dead Channel Video. <strong>TamaMedics</strong> is a preservation and research effort. <strong>Signalbox</strong> continues useful old open-source software with a modern terminal interface. This node is the map, not a costume borrowed from any of them.</p><p>Smaller builds and notes are filed on the lab bench as they become coherent.</p></div></WindowPanel>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
